  "description": "NOPNAK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H150 N12 O28 Pr6,2(C6 H6). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr1A (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2A (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr3A (Pr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.033-4.108 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.05-113.19°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Pr6(OH)8(piv)10(deta)4·2C6H6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
